The agent-hooks CLI's stable-names default and its generated-file tracking (the sibling hooks.meta.json sidecar) are the authority for the committed hook manifests, and each committed hooks.json command reference and hooks.meta.json files list must match what a fresh build emits — the manifest is a pure function of its inputs, so an unchanged rebuild writes identical bytes and the host's hook-trust hash survives. Changing the bundle-naming, pruning, or sidecar behavior without regenerating the manifests silently breaks the plugins' hook wiring, as the pre-1.7 hash-named bundles did for three months.
